# Gev, Scaled Scorch cares whether an opponent lost life this turn, not how their life total changed (the ruling; CR 119.3). In
# turn 3 Gev attacks and Bot2 blocks with a Healer's Hawk: the Hawk's lifelink gains Bot2 1 life (21) and the Hawk dies. In the
# second main phase Bot1 casts Magebane Lizard, a Lizard spell: Gev deals 1 damage to Bot2 (back to 20, the life total it began the
# turn with), and the Lizard, entering after that, gets one +1/+1 counter, a 2/5, because Bot2 lost life even though its total
# did not go down. Gev himself, entering before any life was lost, has none.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Gev, Scaled Scorch
Magebane Lizard
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Healer's Hawk
Plains x20

